WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.700
RT-Safe: Benchmarking Agent Safety in Real-Time Embodied Environment.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.700
Conventional static evaluation pauses the world during inference.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.750
But the real world does not stop.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.650
We introduce RT-Safe: the embodied world keeps evolving while the agent thinks.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.500
The same initial scene and commanded move, with different world timing.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.950
Contact interrupts movement in the real-time illustration.

00:00:18.397 --> 00:00:20.152
Our RT-Safe task and environment: navigate to the goal safely.

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:22.130
Avoid collisions.

00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:24.677
Avoid environmental hazards.

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:26.753
Obey traffic rules.

00:00:27.486 --> 00:00:28.816
Reach the goal safely.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.202
How do frontier agents perform?

00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:35.335
On the same recorded route, Astra makes twelve

00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:36.809
decisions with one collision.

00:00:37.492 --> 00:00:40.383
Sol makes thirty-three decisions with seventeen collisions.

00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:42.965
These are original recorded inputs.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.050
All eight models complete over 90% of tasks.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.600
Every model has safe success below 4%.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.100
Sonnet records the fewest collisions; Grok, the most.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.400
Inkling favors longer moves. Response time and action choices shape behavior.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.700
Sonnet responds fastest. Sol makes the most decisions, turns, and waits.

00:00:58.379 --> 00:00:59.781
Task completion is not enough.

00:01:00.369 --> 00:01:02.993
Success reaches ninety-four point four percent, but safe

00:01:03.003 --> 00:01:05.057
success is only zero point seven percent.

00:01:06.392 --> 00:01:10.430
On matched hard routes, real-time collisions rise twelve point three times.

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:13.941
About eighty-four percent occur while the agent is deciding.

00:01:15.397 --> 00:01:17.564
More reasoning is not reliably safer.

00:01:18.307 --> 00:01:21.068
From default to higher effort, collisions rise from

00:01:21.078 --> 00:01:23.588
forty point seven to sixty-two per episode.

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:28.911
RT-Safe supports reinforcement learning with rewards for safety.
